<title>USA: BBN up again as AT&amp;T deal rumor persists.</title>
<headline>BBN up again as AT&amp;T deal rumor persists.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-04-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in Internet service provider BBN Corp rose for a third straight day Monday on speculation that AT&amp;T Corp may bid for BBN.</p>
<p>&quot;The rumor is AT&amp;T making a bid of $26 per share,&quot; a trader said.</p>
<p>Both companies declined comment on the rumors.</p>
<p>At midday on the New York Stock Exchange, BBN was up 1-3/8 to 21-1/2, extending a rise from around 16 that began last Thursday.</p>
<p>Trading volume in BBN has been unusually high over the last three sessions. At midday today NYSE volume topped 435,000 shares, exceeding BBN's average daily volume of about 140,000.  </p>
<p>According to data from S&amp;P MarketScope, BBN has 21.2 million shares outstanding.</p>
<p>((--Wall Street Desk, 212-859-1730))</p>
